' A real, ordinary ArcoBASIC program meant to be compiled BY the Fission
' Compiler Substrate's own native x86-64 backend (fission/amir/lower_x86_64.abas)
' -- see fission/tests/native_programs/hello_native.abas's own header
' comment for the directory convention.
'
' RANGE, Array.Empty/Array.IsEmpty/Array.New, EXIT/ISNULL. RANGE
' materializes a real Array:Number of every value the real range would
' iterate (the oracle's own real RangeValue is a genuinely distinct lazy
' type this backend does not have -- FOR-IN/LEN/indexing all behave
' identically, PRINTing a bare Range value directly does not, not
' exercised here). EXIT/ExitProgram/ExitTheProgram are a real, direct
' `exit(2)` syscall with a real, caller-supplied code.
'
' Real, disclosed, ACCEPTED divergence (the SAME one this backend's own
' NULL-literal support already established, see fission/sir/
' lower_amir.abas's own comment): `ISNULL(0)` is TRUE here but FALSE in
' the oracle -- a real Number 0 and a real NULL are indistinguishable in
' this backend's own representation (every pointer-kind value IS a plain
' integer, and NULL itself lowers to a real `CONST 0`), so this is
' deliberately NOT exercised in this byte-for-byte fixture; ISNULL on a
' genuine NULL, or a genuinely non-zero value, both already match exactly
' and ARE exercised below.
'
' Real, disclosed narrower scope: bare `Exit(code)` as the FIRST token of
' a STATEMENT (not assigned to anything) does not parse -- "EXIT" is
' reserved for loop control (EXIT WHILE/FOR/DO) and the self-hosted
' parser's own statement dispatch only disambiguates it as an ordinary
' callable identifier in EXPRESSION position (already fixed in an earlier
' session, see fission/language/arcobasic/parser.abas's own comment on
' `Fission_ArcoBasicCanName`) -- `ignored = Exit(code)` (the exact form
' every real Fission CLI driver already uses throughout this codebase)
' works correctly and is what this fixture exercises.
'
' Expected output verified against legacy `ArcoFission compile-run` on this
' identical source as the equivalence-testing oracle.
r = Range(1, 10, 2)
FOR x IN r
    PRINT x
NEXT
PRINT LEN(r)

a = Array.New(3, 99)
PRINT a
PRINT Array.Empty(a)
e = Array.New(0, 0)
PRINT Array.Empty(e)
PRINT Array.IsEmpty(e)

PRINT ISNULL(5)
n = NULL
PRINT ISNULL(n)

PRINT "before exit"
ignored = Exit(3)
PRINT "unreachable"
